From b4062c1971ec1c457a4c1d45cefae7f1cd44102d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:24:28 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: stat boosts won by rounds replace the coin stat shop

The story's stat-boost items (Power Bread HP +8, Cookie PP +4, Apple Attack +5,
Hard Nut Defense +3, Mint Agility +4, Lucky Pepper Luck +1; menu/menu/use.c says
which raises what) are no longer given. cupdata.py BOOSTS attaches the ones
from each cup's story stretch to rounds ("boost" rewards, 22 in all); the first
win of the round adds one to a party-wide pool of that stat (a persistent byte
flag per stat at 0x740 + 8 * stat, once-only bits at 0x770 to 0x78f) and the
attendant says "You can boost HP once more!". New reward kind
ARENA_REWARD_BOOST in ArenaSeries_GiveRewards.

The party manager's Stats counter (arena_shop.c) now spends the pool for free:
the tag under each icon and the right window show the boosts left, the price
window the boosts used; a Reset entry gives every applied boost back. Applied
boosts are not stored: Unit_GetLevelBase (levels.c, far call
Unit_GetLevelBaseFar) is the closed form of the base stats from levelling
alone, and a unit's boosts applied = (base stat - that) / the boost's amount;
Reset sets the base stats back to it. The stat icons are fixed to the items'
real stats. Messages above the generated block; gen-cups.py re-run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
